  "claim_short": "Full affirmative solution to Remark 3.6 of arXiv:2405.08416: the L-infinity condition (ii) is redundant in the compact T(1) theorem a la Stein. The normalized-bump L2 decay condition (i) alone implies compactness. A cube-localized cutoff gives MO_Q(T(1)) at most C A^(d/2) epsilon_T(x_Q,A ell(Q)) plus C A^(-delta). Choosing A to tend slowly to infinity proves the small-cube, large-cube, and far-translation CMO...",
